# 
# http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#ActiveDevice
<http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#ActiveDevice> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#ActiveDevice> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#Device> .
<http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#ActiveDevice> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A medical device that depends on a source of electrical energy or any source of power other than that directly generated by the human body or gravity."@en .
<http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#ActiveDevice> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Active Medical Device"@en .
# 
# http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#ActiveImplant
<http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#ActiveImplant> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#ActiveImplant> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#ImplantableDevice> .
<http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#ActiveImplant> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An implantable device that requires a power source (e.g., pacemaker, LVAD, cochlear implant)."@en .
<http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#ActiveImplant> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Active Implantable Device"@en .
# 
# http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#BiomaterialRisk
<http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#BiomaterialRisk> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#BiomaterialRisk> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#Risk> .
<http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#BiomaterialRisk> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Risk related to biomaterial interactions (thrombosis, infection, biocompatibility, allergic reactions)."@en .
<http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#BiomaterialRisk> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Biomaterial Risk"@en .
# 
# http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#ClassI
<http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#ClassI> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#ClassI> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#RiskClass> .
<http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#ClassI> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Lowest risk class. Self-certification by the manufacturer is sufficient (e.g., bandages, wheelchairs)."@en .
<http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#ClassI> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Risk Class I"@en .
# 
# http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#ClassIII
<http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#ClassIII> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#ClassIII> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#RiskClass> .
<http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#ClassIII> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Highest risk class. Requires rigorous Notified Body assessment (e.g., heart valves, pacemakers, LVAD)."@en .
<http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#ClassIII> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Risk Class III"@en .
# 
# http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#ClassIIa
<http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#ClassIIa> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#ClassIIa> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#RiskClass> .
<http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#ClassIIa> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Low to medium risk. Requires Notified Body assessment (e.g., hearing aids, contact lenses)."@en .
<http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#ClassIIa> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Risk Class IIa"@en .
# 
# http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#ClassIIb
<http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#ClassIIb> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#ClassIIb> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#RiskClass> .
<http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#ClassIIb> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Medium to high risk. Requires Notified Body assessment (e.g., ventilators, surgical lasers, infusion pumps)."@en .
<http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#ClassIIb> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Risk Class IIb"@en .
# 
# http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#CorrectiveAction
<http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#CorrectiveAction> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#CorrectiveAction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Any corrective action taken by the manufacturer for technical or medical reasons related to device characteristics (MDR Art. 2.68)."@en .
<http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#CorrectiveAction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Field Safety Corrective Action (FSCA)"@en .
# 
# http://www.uoc.edu/emdco#Country
